course: dictionary
lesson: 15224
title: Sevenfold
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sevenfold means seven times as big or as many. The ending -fold works like times: twofold means two times, threefold means three times, and sevenfold means seven times.
explain: «The price of the sweets rose sevenfold.» The price did not go up a little. It went up seven times. Check by swapping in your meaning: «The price rose seven times» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Sevenfold can also mean having seven parts, and in the Bible it can mean a lot, as in «avenged sevenfold». When you meet it, read the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
fact: Sevenfold means seven times as big or as many.
fact: The ending -fold works like times: twofold, threefold and sevenfold.
fact: «A sevenfold increase» means the number became seven times bigger.
fact: «The town's population grew sevenfold» means it grew to seven times its old size.
fact: Sevenfold can also mean having seven parts, or, in the Bible, seven times over, a lot.
exercise: «The school made a sevenfold increase in library books.» What does sevenfold mean here? | Seven days long | Half as many | Seven pages thick | *Seven times as many
exercise: Which word means seven times over? | sevens | twofold | *sevenfold | seventeen
exercise: Ravi's dad says the rain grew sevenfold overnight. What does grew sevenfold mean? | *It grew seven times as big | It grew by exactly seven centimetres | It stopped completely | It grew smaller
test: «Her savings grew sevenfold in one year.» What does this tell you about her savings? | They stayed the same size | They became seven pounds smaller | They became seven coins heavier | *They became seven times bigger
test: A sevenfold plan is a plan with what? | *Seven parts | One big part | No parts at all | Two parts
exam: In «a sevenfold increase», what does sevenfold mean? | Seven steps up | *Seven times as big | Seven in a row | Less than before
